Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Sun Jun 14 00:58:48 2026 -0400

    fix(#12244) P0: don't resurrect RESTARTING intent across harness restart
    
    A RESTARTING intent is a transient in-flight state owned by the harness
    session that issued it. load_state restored it as-is across a harness
    restart; against an agent whose claude.exe outlived the restart, its stale
    intent_set_at (already past FORCE_KILL_TIMEOUT) made the first health poll
    force-kill a HEALTHY agent, then auto-reboot it — the operator-reported
    'working agent killed + respawned, repeatedly' loop.
    
    Fix: reset RESTARTING->RUNNING (clear intent_set_at) on load_state. A dead
    agent still auto-reboots (RUNNING is in should_reboot); a live one is left
    alone. STOPPING is preserved (an operator stop must survive a restart).
    
    Tests: reset-to-running for legacy (no key) + present-stale-timestamp cases;
    round-trip test retargeted to STOPPING (the intent that DOES survive). 188 passed.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

